  "reason": "Evidence: RNA (PCA n2000, single profile) achieves 0.485 accuracy while image (ResNet50) is weak at 0.208, establishing RNA as the dominant modality. The key uncertainty is whether a learned RNA encoder (scvi_n200) can substantially outperform the simple linear PCA reduction. This experiment (config_004) directly compares scvi_n200 vs PCA n2000 while holding profile setting (single) and model setting (rna_only) constant, cleanly isolating the effect of the RNA representation. If scvi_n200 improves accuracy, it justifies investing further experiments in learned encoders and multimodal fusion with that encoder; if not, PCA is sufficient and we should pivot to testing aggregation (multiprofile) or better image encoders. With 7 experiments remaining, this single-variable comparison is the highest-information next step before committing budget to more complex multimodal configurations."
